# Must-fail mutant for legacy-invoices.schemas.test.ts's AC-10 format split
# (T48), re-aimed at the F2-R contract (rulings.md F2-R, commit 59bf47d59).
#
# Mutates `legacy-invoices.schemas.ts` — removes `format: "date-time"` from the
# two range `create_datetime` operators (`gte`, `lte`), the only two absolute
# leaves that still carry a date-time format after F2-R split eq/gt/lt to
# `format: "date"`. The relative `before`/`after` keys stay format-free (D-19).
#
# Original intent (pre-F2-R): drop the date-time format from the absolute
# create_datetime operators, reddening the AC-10 format assertion. F2-R changed
# three of the five former context lines (eq/gt/lt are now `format: "date"`), so
# the old five-leaf mutation no longer applies. Same intent, new contract: strip
# the format from the two surviving date-time leaves.
#
# **Reddens — confirmed against `legacy-invoices.schemas.test.ts:128`, "@AC-10
# @AC-15 the create_datetime operators split by format: eq/gt/lt declare date,
# gte/lte date-time, before/after none"**: with this patch applied, `formatOf`
# reads `undefined` for gte, so its `.toBe("date-time")` assertion fails (1 of 12
# unit specs reddens, 11 stay green). The :88 datetime-acceptance spec stays
# green — a format-free string still validates the datetime value.
#
# Declared collateral: NONE. Verified against `test:integration legacy-invoices`
# (24 pass) — a format-free gte/lte still passes the criteria gate and reaches
# the wire as a date-time, so the range-format int spec (:138) stays green.
# Re-verified applied-and-reverted; the schema file has no diff after revert.
#
# Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.
